<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kirtivarman I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 566–597</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kirtivarman I was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badami">Badami</a> from about 566 to 597, son of the founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pulakeshin-i">Pulakeshin I</a>. He defeated the Kadambas of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banavasi">Banavasi</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Mauryas</a> of the Konkan and the Nalas, laying the base of Chalukya power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>. After a regency by his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mangalesha">Mangalesha</a>, his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pulakeshin-ii">Pulakeshin II</a> became the dynasty's greatest king.</p></div>
